[00:11.90] She lives her life in honky tonks
[00:15.56] And the crowded back street bar
[00:19.26] A world of make-believe that knows
[00:24.24] No sun, no moon or star
[00:28.00] Just the glitter of the great white way
[00:32.48] And the glare of city light
[00:36.28] Where the music's loud, she's in the crowd
[00:40.78] A lonely girl in the night
[00:44.32] CHORUS:
[00:45.36] I wonder if she's thinking
[00:48.84] Of dreams that didn't last
[00:52.74] I wonder if she's haunted
[00:57.20] By heartaches from the past
[01:01.58] Perhaps there is a story
[01:05.46] Of a love that wasn't right
[01:09.20] Now the shadows hide her empty pride
[01:13.74] A lonely girl in the night
[01:37.58] Spoken:
[01:38.00] I watch her sit there so lonely
[01:40.34] As she lights a cigarette
[01:44.40] And the smoke rings rise, but in her eyes
[01:48.86] Oh, there seems to be such regret
[01:52.40] Is she there to tempt a lover
[01:56.14] In that dress that hugs her tight
[01:59.80] With a glass of wine to pass the time
[02:04.34] Just a lonely girl - in the night
